1B bond comfortably (utility-credit).\n- **Equity is the weak spot.** Two utility share offerings were cut back in size (utility-credit). Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short (pellham-offering).\n- **Pellham is the constrained case.** Its 2027 capex is planned up 18%, and Norvane's up 12% (utility-capex-2027). Pellham has said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves (pellham-offering). That suggests it can't close the gap with debt alone, probably because of leverage and credit-rating limits. The sources don't say this directly, so it's my inference.\n- **Knock-on effect.** Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria (utility-capex-2027). Its cuts will hit transformer and substation suppliers.\n\n**Caveat:** I found no data on individual balance sheets, rating headroom or the total size of the funding gap. The Pellham–Norvane split rests on one bond deal and one failed equity raise.","ttft_ms":5224,"type":"result","duration_ms":24415,"uuid":"eb3c3479-0a7b-49fd-9445-0f5597a3b563","ttft_stream_ms":4991,"time_to_request_ms":72,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":22,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":68,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":203,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":130,"process_rss_mib_result":203,"process_anon_mib_result":122,"process_peak_rss_mib":222,"process_cpu_ms_turn":661,"process_wall_ms_turn":244